      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm real worried about a heifer I just had a rumenotomy on. She seems alright on the outside, but I can't help feeling like there's something nasty lurking deep inside her rumen that I just can't see. I'm terrified that some kind of infection or a pocket of pus is sneaking around in there in the dark, hidden from view, just waiting to take over.\n\nWhat are the actual signs that an unseen infection or some kind of nasty intruder like an abscess is festering deep in the abdomen? And how can I tell if something is actually in there, lurking in the shadows of her gut, before it's too late? Please be specific with the clinical signs.",
